  "bodyText": "Home\nVisit Us\nExhibitions\nEvents\nOnline Talks\nOxfordshire’s Military Heritage in 50 Objects\nCollections\nBlog\nResearch\nLearning\nShop\nCart\nMy Account\nAbout\nBecome a Friend\nSupport Us\nRoom Hire\n\n01993 810 210\n\nfrontofhouse@sofo.org.uk\n\n  \nHome\nEvents\nExhibitions\nCollections\nFriends’ Membership\nVisit\nShop\nBasket\nMy Account\nOxfordshire’s Military Heritage in 50 Objects\nResearch\nLearning\nOnline Talks\nBlog\nSupport Us\nRoom Hire\nImage Services\nAbout\nBooks\nGifts\nThe Oxfordshire Light Infantry Chronicle 1897\n£40.00\n\nSorry, this item is out of stock\n\nCompiled and Edited by Captain A. F. Mockler-Ferryman\n\nPublished 1898 - Eyre and Spottiswoode, London\n\n \n\nContents:\n\nRegimental Calendar for 1898\nThe Army List January 1897\nThe Army List November 1897\nThe 1st Battalion in 1897\nRecord of The 1st Battalion 1897\nThe 2nd Battalion in 1897\nRecord of the 2nd Battalion in 1897\nThe Depot in 1897\nExtracts from the London Gazette in 1887\nChanges in Equipment in 1897\nOfficers Dress Regulation 1897\nMusketry 1897\nAthletics in 1897\nFootball in 1897\nCricket in 1897\nSignalling in 1897\nThe 43rd Light Infantry Dinner 1897\nThe 52nd Light Infantry Dinner 1897\nThe Indian Frontier Campaign\n- The Mohmand expedition\n- Peshawar Column (Tirah Expeditionary Column)\n\nMiscellaneous\n\nMajor General McPherson\nSir Martin Hunter\nA Letter from Sir John Moore\nCaptain John Dodd’s Narrative of The Peninsular War\nWar Medals\nFullers Hoek 1852\nThrough the Centre of India with the 43rd 1857-58\nA 52nd Letter 1862\nPig Sticking in 1897\nThe Essentials of Good Skirmishing\nObituaries\n\nIllustrations\n\nMaps\n\n \n\nPlease Note: Original copies supplied, all in used but reasonable condition. Copy supplied may vary slightly from the one pictured in terms of wear and aging.\n\n \n\nRelated products\nThe Royal Green Jackets Chronicle 1970\n£3.00 Add to cart\nBugle & Sabre VI\n£5.00 Read more\nThe Story of the Oxfordshire Yeomanry – Queen’s Own Oxfordshire Hussars 1798-1998\n£7.95 Read more\nBugle & Sabre II\n£5.00 Add to cart\n\nSoldiers of Oxfordshire Museum\nPark Street.\nWoodstock\nOxfordshire OX20 1SN\n\nPhone and Email:\nGeneral Enquiries & Event Tickets: 01993 810 211\nfrontofhouse@sofo.org.uk\n\nPrivacy Policy\nTerms and conditions",
